atlas surface

architecture account-device-keys
  canonical_name AccountDeviceKeys
  family surface
  domain Surface / Account Devices
  layer surface/account
  semantic_question Which devices has this person named on their account, with which public key fingerprints, and which have they revoked?
  purpose Owns /account/devices: a signed-in person records a device by name and the public key fingerprint they type, and revokes it later. Rows are device_key CMS records keyed by the account subject (user:N), written only through the CMS binary. auth.db is not touched.
  maturity implemented
  consumes BonfyreAuth
  publishes DeviceKey
  node_types DeviceKey
  edge_types names_device
  invariant the account subject comes from a verified BonfyreAuth session, never from a form field
  invariant every enroll or revoke is the person's own same-origin form submit; a cross-site submit is refused and writes nothing
  invariant attestation is always recorded as "not verified"; no hardware check runs
  invariant a revoke is a compare-and-set on the person's own published row; another account's id is refused
  forbidden_inference an enrolled device key -> hardware attestation, a secure-element key, or proof the device exists
  forbidden_inference an enrolled device key -> a credential accepted at sign-in
  known_gap no attestation verifier exists; the Stitch screen's checklist (enclave, biometric) is shown as not verified
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/device_key.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/account_continuity_web.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/account_continuity_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/account_continuity_test.sh enrolls a device through the form, reads the row back as "not verified", proves a cross-site enroll writes nothing, a stranger cannot see or revoke it, and the owner's revoke archives it

architecture account-device-move
  canonical_name AccountDeviceMove
  family surface
  domain Surface / Account Devices
  layer surface/account
  semantic_question Has this account offered a one-use code to take its own site export onto another device, and has a device signed in to the same account used it?
  purpose Owns /account/move (sender) and /account/move/receive (receiver). The sender's submit creates a device_pairing record holding only a digest of a six-digit code bound to the account subject and the offering session's digest, open for ten minutes; a new offer withdraws older open ones. The receiver, signed in to the same account, submits the code; a compare-and-set marks it received once and the page offers download links to that account's existing /cms/compose/export. Nothing is pushed.
  maturity implemented
  consumes BonfyreAuth
  consumes PageComposition
  publishes DevicePairing
  node_types DevicePairing
  edge_types offers_copy
  invariant nothing transfers without two explicit submits: the sender offers the code, the receiver enters it, and the download is the receiver's own click on the existing export route
  invariant the code is shown once and never stored; only a digest of account subject and code is kept
  invariant a code is redeemable only by the same account subject, only while offered and unexpired, and only once
  invariant the export downloaded is the account's own /cms/compose/export, authorised by that route's own ownership check
  forbidden_inference a received pairing -> a completed transfer, a trusted device, a second session or a copied credential
  forbidden_inference a pairing code -> peer-to-peer, LAN or enclave transport; the copy is an ordinary HTTPS download
  known_gap the Stitch screens show a LAN/P2P stream with progress; there is no such transport, so the page shows the export manifest and download links only
  known_gap session_handoff_web.h's one-use nonce is bound to a territory handoff in BonfyreAuth, not to an export; it was not reused because doing so needs an auth.db schema change
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/device_pairing.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/account_continuity_web.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/account_continuity_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/account_continuity_test.sh offers a code, proves it is not stored in clear, a stranger cannot redeem it, a second session of the same account redeems it once, and a reuse is refused

architecture bluesky-sync-request
  canonical_name BlueskySyncRequest
  family surface
  domain Surface / Connected Identities
  layer surface/account
  semantic_question Has this person asked for the public repository behind a Bluesky handle they declared to be read, and has anything run?
  purpose Owns /connections/bluesky/sync: for each Bluesky link the person declared through BonfyreAuth external-link-claim, a submit records a carrier_sync_request with run_state requested. No AT Protocol reader exists, so the page states requested and not run.
  maturity implemented
  consumes BonfyreAuth
  publishes CarrierSyncRequest
  node_types CarrierSyncRequest
  edge_types requests_sync
  invariant only a link returned by external-link-list for the signed-in session can be named; another account's link is refused
  invariant a request is never shown as fetched, verified or synced; run_state stays requested until an executor exists and writes otherwise
  forbidden_inference a sync request -> a fetched repository, a CAR file, MST verification, or that the handle belongs to the person
  forbidden_inference a sync request -> permission to post on the person's behalf
  known_gap there is no AT Protocol / CAR sync executor anywhere in the estate; requests accumulate unrun
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/carrier_sync_request.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/account_continuity_web.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/account_continuity_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/account_continuity_test.sh shows the empty state, declares a handle through BonfyreAuth, refuses a stranger's request for it, records the owner's request and shows "requested · not run"

architecture feed-agent-policy
  canonical_name FeedAgentPolicy
  family surface
  domain Surface / Connected Identities
  layer surface/account
  semantic_question For each feed this person keeps, which named agent or MCP client may read it, and how much?
  purpose Owns /account/agents: per saved_item collection the person keeps and per agent name they type, a feed_agent_policy row with access read, summary or none, updated in place. No MCP tool or /connect path serves saved feeds today, so the rule is recorded and the page says it is not enforced.
  maturity implemented
  consumes SavedItem
  consumes BonfyreAuth
  publishes FeedAgentPolicy
  node_types FeedAgentPolicy
  edge_types governs_agent_read
  invariant a rule can be set only on a feed (saved_item collection) the signed-in account keeps
  invariant one rule per account, feed and agent name: the policy id is a digest of the three, and a change updates that row
  invariant a missing rule means no access for any future read path
  forbidden_inference a feed rule -> that an agent has read or can read the feed today
  forbidden_inference an agent name -> the identity or operator of a client
  known_gap no MCP or /connect read path serves saved feeds, so there is nothing to wire the check into; site_mcp.c serves public site posts, which stay public and are not governed by this rule
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/feed_agent_policy.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/account_continuity_web.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/account_continuity_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/account_continuity_test.sh refuses a rule from an account that does not keep the feed, records the owner's rule and updates it in place, and shows "Not yet" for enforcement

architecture field-dispatch
  canonical_name FieldDispatch
  family surface
  domain Surface / Field Work
  layer surface/account
  semantic_question Who asked for a visit to which place at what time for what need, who was it offered to, and did they accept?
  purpose Owns /dispatch: a signed-in person records a field request (place, time, need); offers it to one published member address, resolved through site_presentation and the matrix to that member's person subject; the named member accepts or declines with their own submit; the requester may withdraw. Rows are field_dispatch CMS records.
  maturity implemented
  consumes BonfyreAuth
  consumes PageComposition
  publishes FieldDispatch
  node_types FieldDispatch
  edge_types offers_visit
  invariant only the requester may offer or withdraw; only the account behind the named member address may accept or decline
  invariant every state change is a compare-and-set on the state the actor saw: requested or declined -> offered -> accepted | declined; open -> withdrawn
  invariant nobody is notified and nothing is booked, contracted or paid; the page says so
  forbidden_inference an accepted field request -> a booking, an employment or service contract, a payment, or a safety check of either person
  forbidden_inference an offered request -> that the member was told about it
  known_gap a member without a published member address cannot be offered a request; NFC, LoRa, scale and handshake tools on the Stitch screen have no device owner and are not shown
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/field_dispatch.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/field_dispatch_web.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/account_continuity_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/account_continuity_test.sh records a request, refuses a stranger's offer, offers it to robin.aurekai.work, refuses the requester's own accept, lets the named member see and accept it, and refuses the member's withdraw

interaction account-continuity-writes-through-cms
  source account-device-keys
  destination cmd-c-m-s
  relation writes_records
  preserves account subject from a verified session, the person's typed values, compare-and-set preconditions
  drops session tokens, pairing codes in clear, any value not submitted by the person
  forbidden_inference a CMS row written here -> verification, transfer, sync or enforcement beyond what its state field says
  invalidates_on device_key, device_pairing, carrier_sync_request, feed_agent_policy, field_dispatch rows; BonfyreAuth session validity
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/account_continuity_test.sh

interaction device-move-reads-site-export
  source account-device-move
  destination page-composition
  relation links_export
  preserves the account's own member sites and the existing /cms/compose/export ownership check
  drops other accounts' sites, credentials
  forbidden_inference a download link -> a completed or verified copy on the receiving device
  invalidates_on site_presentation and site_page rows for the account
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/account_continuity_test.sh

interaction field-dispatch-writes-through-cms
  source field-dispatch
  destination cmd-c-m-s
  relation writes_records
  preserves requester and assignee subjects, the stated place, time and need, explicit answers
  drops notifications, prices, schedules beyond the stated time
  forbidden_inference a field_dispatch row -> a booking or payment
  invalidates_on field_dispatch rows; site_presentation for the named address
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/account_continuity_test.sh
